{
  "slug": "secure-sdlc-agents",
  "name": "Secure Sdlc Agents",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A team of 8 AI security specialists embedded in your coding workflow — covering every phase of the Software Development Lifecycle. Includes AppSec Engineer, GRC Analyst, Cloud/Platform Engineer, Dev Lead, Release Manager, Security Champion, Product Manager, and AI Security Engineer. Each agent is invoked at the exact phase where their expertise prevents real vulnerabilities: STRIDE threat modelling, ASVS-mapped requirements, IaC security review, SAST triage, compliance attestation, and pre-release security gating. Works with Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, Warp, and any MCP-compatible tool.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills** and **8 agents**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `ai-security` (Use when building any feature that calls an LLM API, processes user input sent to a model, uses…), `compliance-and-audit` (Use when a project requires a compliance framework mapping, when risks need formal documentation, when audit evidence must…), `security-and-hardening` (Use when writing or reviewing code that handles user input, authentication, access control, cryptography, error handling, file uploads,…), `threat-modeling` (Use when a new feature, architecture, or significant design decision is being made)\n- **Agents** (8): `ai-security-engineer` (AI/LLM Security Engineer), `appsec-engineer` (Application Security Engineer), `cloud-platform-engineer` (Cloud and Platform Security Engineer), `dev-lead` (Secure Development Lead), `grc-analyst` (Governance, Risk and Compliance Analyst), `product-manager` (Secure Product Manager), `release-manager` (Security-focused Release Manager), `security-champion` (Security Champion — a developer-level security advocate embedded in the squad)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install secure-sdlc-agents@claude-community` from `Kaademos/secure-sdlc-agents`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 4,
    "agent": 8
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
